WEBVTT

00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:08.470
You can use Line Select as a guest, but signing in lets your pack, your interview and your rankings follow you to any device.

00:00:08.470 --> 00:00:13.271
Create an account with your email and a password, and agree to the terms.

00:00:13.271 --> 00:00:20.768
You'll get a recovery code once — save it somewhere, because it gets you back in if you ever forget your password.

00:00:21.987 --> 00:00:27.584
Then load your bid pack: the same PDF you download for your domicile, aircraft and month.

00:00:27.584 --> 00:00:34.376
Drop it on the page or choose the file. Line Select reads the pairings and the line grids straight from it —

00:00:34.376 --> 00:00:39.974
nothing is typed in by hand — and it never keeps other pilots' names or employee numbers.

00:00:40.675 --> 00:00:45.140
It shows you what it found: how many lines, the credit, the days off.

00:00:45.140 --> 00:00:49.542
If the PDF has both captain and first officer lines, pick your seat.

00:00:49.542 --> 00:00:51.613
If it all looks right, continue.

00:00:54.468 --> 00:01:05.076
Just want a look first? "Try it with sample data" loads a small made-up pack, clearly marked as the sample, so you can try everything before your own pack is out.

